# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform. This is
# not a style preference: reference.json is a byte contract that
# `gen-reference verify` compares byte-for-byte, and the Rust sources and
# fixtures are embedded or hashed from the working tree, so a CRLF checkout
# (Windows autocrlf) would silently change what is verified.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures whose bytes are part of the test contract.
*.gz binary
